          %ul
            %li#CiracZoller95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Ignacio+Cirac"}> J. Ignacio Cirac
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Zoller"} Peter Zoller
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Computations with Cold Trapped Ions
              %strong 74
              (1995) 4091 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.74.4091"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.74.4091
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Quantum computing became widely thought to be not just a theoretical but a plausible practical possibility with the theoretical understanding of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correction"} quantum error correction
            (which however remains to be implemented scalably):
          %ul
