                = succeed "," do
                  %em Physicists in China challenge Google’s “quantum advantage”
                %strong 588
                380 (2020) (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-020-03434-7"}> doi:10.1038/d41586-020-03434-7
                )
            %li#DasSarma22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sankar+Das+Sarma"}> Sankar Das Sarma
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum computing has a hype problem
                %a{:href => "https://www.technologyreview.com/2022/03/28/1048355/quantum-computing-has-a-hype-problem/"} MIT Technology Review (March 2022)
              %blockquote
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qubit"} qubit
                  systems we have today are a tremendous scientific achievement, but they take us no closer to having a quantum computer that can solve a problem that anybody cares about.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
                  What is missing is the breakthrough
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
                  bypassing
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correction"} quantum error correction
                  by using far-more-stable qubits, in an approach called
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+computing"} topological quantum computing
          %p
            Potential relation to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Unruh+effect"} Unruh effect
          %ul
            %li
              Eric W. Aspling, John A. Marohn, Michael J. Lawler,
              %em Design Constraints for Unruh-DeWitt Quantum Computers
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.12552"}> arXiv:2210.12552
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %div
            %h3#quantum_programming_languages Quantum programming languages
            %p The first proposal towards formalizing quantum programming languages was:
            %ul
              %li#Knill96
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emanuel+Knill"}> Emanuel Knill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conventions for quantum pseudocode
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.osti.gov/biblio/366453-conventions-quantum-pseudocode"} LA-UR-96-2724
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2172/366453"} doi:10.2172/366453
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/366453"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Knill-QuantumPseudocode.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              and early formalization via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+lambda-calculus"} quantum lambda-calculus
              invoking
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear types
              (cf.
              %a{:href => "#Pratt92"} Pratt 1992
              etc.):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beno%C3%AEt+Valiron"}> Benoît Valiron
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A functional programming language for quantum computation with classical control
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.20381/ruor-18372"} doi:10.20381/ruor-18372
                  %a{:href => "https://ruor.uottawa.ca/bitstream/10393/26790/1/MR01625.PDF"} pdf
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#SelingerValiron04
                %p
