                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/cs/0404056"} arXiv:cs/0404056
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/11417170_26"} doi:10.1007/11417170_26
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#SelingerValiron09
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Selinger"}> Peter Selinger
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beno%C3%AEt+Valiron"} Benoît Valiron
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Quantum Lambda Calculus
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Semantic Techniques in Quantum Computation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139193313.005"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139193313.005
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mscs.dal.ca/~selinger/papers/qlambdabook.pdf"} pdf
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %blockquote
              %p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "Quipper#Selinger16"}> Selinger (2016)
                \:&amp;rbrack; When the
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathstat.dal.ca/~selinger/qpl/"} QPL workshop series
                was first founded, it was called “
                %em> Quantum Programming Languages
                ”. One year I wasn’t participating, and while I wasn’t looking they changed the name to “
                %em> Quantum Physics and Logic
                ” — same acronym!
              %p
                Back in those days in the early 21st century we were actually trying to do programming languages for quantum computing
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "#SelingerValiron04"} Selinger &amp; Valiron 2004
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              %p
                Now it’s 15 years later and several of these parameters have changed: There has been a renewed interest, from government agencies and also from companies who are actually building quantum computers.
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo .
                        %mo .
                        %mo .
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              %p
                So now people are working on quantum programming languages
                = succeed "." do
                  %em again
            %p
              Exposition of the general idea of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+languages"} quantum programming languages
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classically+controlled+quantum+computation"} classically controlled quantum computation
              with an eye towards the
