                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnmrs.2024.02.002"}> doi:10.1016/j.pnmrs.2024.02.002
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.01308"} arXiv:2402.01308
                %blockquote
                  %p “Nuclear magnetic resonance is arguably both the best available quantum technology for implementing simple quantum computing experiments and the worst technology for building large scale quantum computers that has ever been seriously put forward. After a few years of rapid growth, leading to an implementation of Shor’s quantum factoring algorithm in a seven-spin system, the field started to reach its natural limits and further progress became challenging. […] the user friendliness of NMR implementations means that they remain popular for proof-of-principle demonstrations of simple quantum information protocols.”
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Wikipedia,
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spin_qubit_quantum_computer"} Spin qbit quantum computer
              %li
                %p
                  Wikipedia,
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_magnetic_resonance_quantum_computer"} Nuclear magnetic resonance quantum computer
            %p
              More on implementation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic+gates"} quantum logic gates
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbits"} qbits
              realized on
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleon"} nucleon
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin"} spin
            %ul
              %li
                Price, Somaroo, Tseng, Gore, Fahmy,, Havel, Cory:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Construction and Implementation of NMR Quantum Logic Gates for Two Spin Systems
                %strong 140
                2 (1999) 371-378
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/jmre.1999.1851"} doi;10.1006/jmre.1999.1851
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              and analogously on
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin"} spin
            %ul
              %li
                M. Yu. Volkov and K. M. Salikhov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Pulse Protocols for Quantum Computing with Electron Spins as Qubits
                %strong 41
                (2011) 145–154
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00723-011-0297-2"} doi:10.1007/s00723-011-0297-2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              For references on spin resonance qbits realized on a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nitrogen-vacancy+center+in+diamond"} nitrogen-vacancy center in diamond
            %p
              There exist toy desktop
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computers"} quantum computers
              for educational purposes, operating on a couple of nuclear magnetic resonance
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbits"} qbits
              at room temperature :
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://en.ciqtek.com/"}> CIQTEK
                  \:
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://en.ciqtek.com/products/detail/diamond-quantum-computer-for-education.html?id=644102ee-942e-4568-aacd-20241a1a2469&id=644102ee-942e-4568-aacd-20241a1a2469"} Diamond Quantum Computer for Education
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://www.spinquanta.com/"}> SpinQ
                  \:
                  %em SpinQ Triangulum: a commercial three-qubit desktop quantum computer
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.02983"} arXiv:2202.02983
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %div
            %h3#SuperconductingQBitsReferences Superconducting qbits
            %p
              On realizing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbits"} qbits
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gates"} quantum gates
              (hence
              = succeed ")" do
